exports[`help command > env help output snapshots > env pull help output snapshots > env pull help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel env pull [filename] [options]
Pull Environment Variables into a local file (default: .env.local)

Options:
  --deployment <DEPLOYMENT>        Pull Environment Variables for a specific deployment (e.g. dpl_xxx)
  -e, --environment <ENVIRONMENT>  Select the environment to pull (default: development)
  --git-branch <BRANCH>            Specify the Git branch to pull specific Environment Variables for
  -p, --project <NAME_OR_ID>       Project name or ID (default: linked project)
  -y, --yes                        Skip the confirmation prompt when overwriting an existing file

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Pull Development Environment Variables into a custom file (check .gitignore)
    vercel env pull <file>

