Options:
  -a, --all             Lists all resources regardless of project
  --integration <NAME>  Limits the resources listed to a designated integration
  --json                Output as JSON

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  List resources for the current linked project
    vercel integration list

  Filter the resources to a single integration
    vercel integration list --integration <integration>

  List all marketplace resources for the current team
    vercel integration list --all
    vercel integration list -a

  List resources as JSON
    vercel integration list --json
"
`;

exports[`help command > integration help output snapshots > integration remove subcommand > integration remove subcommand help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel integration remove <integration> [options]
Remove a marketplace integration. Resources must be deleted first using \`integration resource delete\`.

Options:
  --json     Output as JSON
  -y, --yes  Skip the confirmation prompt when removing an integration

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Remove an integration
    vercel integration remove <integration>

  Delete a resource before removing the integration
    vercel integration resource delete <resource-name> --disconnect-all --yes

  Output as JSON
    vercel integration remove acme --json --yes
"
`;

exports[`help command > integration help output snapshots > integration update subcommand > integration update subcommand help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel integration update <integration> [options]
Update a marketplace integration installation (billing plan or which projects can access it). Install, remove, and
connect flows are separate (integration add, integration remove, integration resource, env pull, etc.) — not part of
update. UI-only flows (OAuth in a browser, consent screens, marketplace purchase) may not map one-to-one to a single CLI
option; pass --billing-plan and --authorization when the product requires them for billing changes. Any extra fields on
the configuration resource that the API exposes but this command PATCH body does not send are not covered until the API
and CLI support them.

Options:
  --authorization <AUTHORIZATION>  Billing authorization ID when the platform requires it for plan changes
  --billing-plan <BILLING_PLAN>    Billing plan ID for integrations that support installation-level billing plans
  --installation <INSTALLATION>    Configuration ID when multiple marketplace installations exist for this integration
  --json                           Output as JSON
  --projects <PROJECT>             Project ID allowed to use this installation, or "all" for all projects (repeatable)

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Grant all team projects access to the integration
    vercel integration update <integration> --projects all

  Limit access to specific projects
    vercel integration update neon --projects prj_abc --projects prj_def

  Change installation billing plan
    vercel integration update acme --billing-plan pro

  Select installation when several exist
    vercel integration update neon --installation icfg_xxx --projects all

  Output result as JSON
    vercel integration update neon --projects all --json

  Non-interactive (JSON success and errors on stdout)
    vercel integration update neon --projects all --non-interactive
"
`;

exports[`help command > integration-resource help output snapshots > integration-resource create-threshold subcommand > integration-resource create-threshold subcommand help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel integration-resource create-threshold <resource> <minimum> <spend> <limit> [options]
Creates a threshold for a resource (or installation, if the integration uses installation-level thresholds)

Options:
  -y, --yes  Skip the confirmation prompt when creating a threshold

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Create a resource threshold
    vercel integration resource create-threshold <resource> <minimum> <spend> <limit>

  Create a resource threshold without confirmation
    vercel integration resource create-threshold <resource> <minimum> <spend> <limit> --yes
"
`;

exports[`help command > integration-resource help output snapshots > integration-resource delete subcommand > integration-resource delete subcommand help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel integration-resource delete <resource> [options]
Delete an integration resource

Options:
  --disconnect-all  Disconnects all projects from the specified resource before deletion
  --json            Output as JSON
  -y, --yes         Skip the confirmation prompt when deleting a resource

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Delete a resource
    vercel integration resource delete <resource>

  Disconnect all projects from a resource, then delete it
    vercel integration resource delete <resource> --disconnect-all

  Output as JSON
    vercel integration resource delete my-acme-resource --json --yes
"
`;

exports[`help command > integration-resource help output snapshots > integration-resource disconnect subcommand > integration-resource disconnect subcommand help column width 120 1`] = `
"▲ vercel integration-resource disconnect <resource> [project] [options]
Disconnect a marketplace resource from a project without deleting the resource

Options:
  --all      Disconnects all projects from the specified resource
  --json     Output as JSON
  -y, --yes  Skip the confirmation prompt when disconnecting a resource

Global Options: See \`vercel --help\`

Examples:
  Disconnect a resource from the current project
    vercel integration resource disconnect <resource>

  Disconnect all projects from a resource
    vercel integration resource disconnect <resource> --all

  Disconnect a resource from a specified project
    vercel integration resource disconnect <resource> <project>

  Output as JSON
    vercel integration resource disconnect my-acme-resource --json --yes
"
`;

